WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:35.041


2
00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:38.250
<b>Arjun has refused to fight the war,</b>

3
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.583
<b>he has already said</b>

4
00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:44.416
<b>that against his elders like Pitamah, Guru Drona,</b>
<b>and his relatives on the enemy side,</b>

5
00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:47.041
<b>he will not be able to raise weapons.</b>

6
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:52.541
<b>Listening to these words,</b>
<b>Lord Sri Krishna smilingly says,</b>

7
00:00:52.541 --> 00:00:54.000
<b>"O Arjun,</b>

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.958
<b>you certainly speak like</b>
<b>the wise and the learne</b>

9
00:00:57.958 --> 00:00:58.708
<b>but</b>

10
00:00:58.708 --> 00:01:04.708
<b>those things for which you express so much</b>
<b>grief are not at all worthy of grief.</b>

11
00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:07.333
<b>Those who truly possess knowledge</b>

12
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:11.750
<b>do not grieve for either the living or the dead."</b>

13
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.333
<b>Arjun has already surrendered</b>
<b>before Sri Krishna,</b>

14
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:18.833
<b>accepting him as his guru and</b>
<b>coming under his shelter,</b>

15
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:26.041
<b>and now here Lord Sri Krishna is beginning</b>
<b>to teach Arjun like a disciple.</b>

16
00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:30.875


17
00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:33.208
<b>When a disciple is immersed in grief,</b>

18
00:01:33.208 --> 00:01:35.500
<b>in emotional turmoil,</b>

19
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:44.583
<b>we usually expect a guru, a teacher, or an</b>
<b>experienced guide to be compassionate,</b>

20
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:50.375
<b>conveying everything with</b>
<b>great sensitivity and solace.</b>

21
00:01:50.375 --> 00:01:51.041
<b>But here,</b>

22
00:01:51.041 --> 00:01:55.166
<b>no consolation is seen in Sri Krishna's tone.</b>

23
00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:58.791
<b>He has made it clear to</b>
<b>Arjun in no uncertain terms</b>

24
00:01:58.791 --> 00:02:02.666
<b>that while his choice of words is</b>
<b>certainly like that of the wise,</b>

25
00:02:02.666 --> 00:02:03.583
<b>but </b>

26
00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:06.875
<b>his statements lack the true wisdom</b>

27
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:08.125
<b>which says that</b>

28
00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:13.000
<b>grieving for either the living or the dead is futile.</b>

29
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.375
<b>Krishna's use of such stern words is</b>
<b>only for Arjun's benefit.</b>

30
00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:20.333
<b>Arjun, unknowingly, clothes his dejection</b>
<b>over not being able to fight the war</b>

31
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:27.375
<b>in such knowledgeable words,</b>
<b>trying to conceal it.</b>

32
00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:29.750
<b>In this emotional delusion,</b>

33
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.291
<b>Arjun is forgetting</b>

34
00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:33.833
<b>the situation that is transient,</b>

35
00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:35.958
<b>the event that is transient,</b>

36
00:02:35.958 --> 00:02:39.083
<b>the human and his body that is transient,</b>

37
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:44.666
<b>a true scholar does not grieve for</b>
<b>such temporary things.</b>

38
00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:49.041
<b>So is concern for the lives of</b>
<b>one's kinsmen also futile? </b>

39
00:02:49.041 --> 00:02:49.916
<b>Perhaps</b>

40
00:02:49.916 --> 00:02:53.833
<b>such questions are also arising in your mind,</b>

41
00:02:53.833 --> 00:02:56.458
<b>that thinking in this way is absolutely wrong.</b>

42
00:02:56.458 --> 00:02:57.791
<b>Don't worry,</b>

43
00:02:57.791 --> 00:02:59.125
<b>stay with me.</b>

44
00:02:59.125 --> 00:03:00.291
<b>In the upcoming verses,</b>

45
00:03:00.291 --> 00:03:01.333
<b>Sri Krishna</b>

46
00:03:01.333 --> 00:03:06.250
<b>will now expose the difference between</b>
<b>this material body and the soul.</b>

47
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.208
<b>He will tell about</b>

48
00:03:07.208 --> 00:03:09.958
<b>the eternity of the soul.</b>

49
00:03:09.958 --> 00:03:15.791
<b>In these teachings of the Gita, you will find</b>
<b>the answer to your every question.</b>

50
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.750


51
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:28.625
<b>This is not the time for words of consolation or</b>
<b>gentle words with Arjun.</b>

52
00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:35.416
<b>It is necessary to shake him awake from the</b>
<b>delusion he is getting entangled in.</b>

53
00:03:35.416 --> 00:03:40.875
<b>That's why my words here are also stern.</b>

54
00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:43.416
<b>The talk of right and wrong,</b>

55
00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:45.583
<b>the talk of virtue and sin,</b>

56
00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:50.333
<b>the talk of fear of the destruction of the lineage</b>

57
00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:55.291
<b>Arjun's choice of words is certainly like</b>
<b>that of the learned,</b>

58
00:03:55.291 --> 00:03:58.375
<b>but at this moment, his conduct</b>

59
00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:00.916
<b>is full of ignorance.</b>

60
00:04:00.916 --> 00:04:02.833
<b>Arjun is trying,</b>

61
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:04.583
<b>making every effort,</b>

62
00:04:04.583 --> 00:04:10.333
<b>just so that somehow he doesn't</b>
<b>have to fight this war,</b>

63
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:14.333
<b>and for this reason, not only to me,</b>

64
00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:19.208
<b>but he is giving all these grand arguments</b>
<b>to himself as well.</b>

65
00:04:19.208 --> 00:04:23.291
<b>This often happens with humans,</b>

66
00:04:23.291 --> 00:04:25.458
<b>when there is insecurity in the mind,</b>

67
00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:28.333
<b>there is helplessness and fear,</b>

68
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:29.083
<b>but</b>

69
00:04:29.083 --> 00:04:34.500
<b>on the surface, he tries to hide all of these,</b>

70
00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:43.708
<b>and in such a situation, he uses words filled</b>
<b>with knowledge, teachings read in books.</b>

71
00:04:43.708 --> 00:04:44.916
<b>The superficial words</b>

72
00:04:44.916 --> 00:04:46.166
<b>and the superficial clothes,</b>

73
00:04:46.166 --> 00:04:47.666
<b>both look resolved,</b>

74
00:04:47.666 --> 00:04:50.833
<b>beautiful,</b>

75
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:54.666
<b>but inside there are many creases, </b>

76
00:04:54.666 --> 00:04:57.500
<b>there is a lack of knowledge.</b>

77
00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.375
<b>This happens</b>

78
00:04:59.375 --> 00:05:00.708
<b>because many times</b>

79
00:05:00.708 --> 00:05:02.416
<b>we read the words,</b>

80
00:05:02.416 --> 00:05:04.375
<b>we memorize the books,</b>

81
00:05:04.375 --> 00:05:05.583
<b>but</b>

82
00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:12.416
<b>the message that lies between</b>
<b>those words and pages,</b>

83
00:05:12.416 --> 00:05:15.125
<b>we are not able to internalize the essence of it.</b>

84
00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:16.250
<b>But</b>

85
00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:20.000
<b>how to recognize this state?</b>

86
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:25.375
<b>A very big indication of this is your state of mind.</b>

87
00:05:25.375 --> 00:05:28.291
<b>If there is certainty in the words,</b>

88
00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:28.916
<b>but</b>

89
00:05:28.916 --> 00:05:31.916
<b>the state of mind is utterly distressed,</b>

90
00:05:31.916 --> 00:05:33.250
<b>then it is time</b>

91
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:37.291
<b>to review your external and internal condition,</b>

92
00:05:37.291 --> 00:05:40.541
<b>perhaps it is also time for a pause.</b>

93
00:05:40.541 --> 00:05:44.541
<b>It is time to take counsel from someone.</b>

94
00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:49.083


95
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:51.000
<b>Arjuna is a wise man,</b>

96
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.541
<b>and his words do not contradict the</b>
<b>teachings written in the sacred scriptures.</b>

97
00:05:57.541 --> 00:06:02.083
<b>So, where is he going wrong?</b>

98
00:06:02.083 --> 00:06:07.083
<b>The fundamental basis of</b>
<b>his arguments is flawed.</b>

99
00:06:07.083 --> 00:06:09.916
<b>You also must have studied mathematics,</b>

100
00:06:09.916 --> 00:06:12.416
<b>where a similar situation arises.</b>

101
00:06:12.416 --> 00:06:17.041
<b>Sometimes, even when our entire process</b>
<b>of reaching the answer is correct,</b>

102
00:06:17.041 --> 00:06:20.875
<b>and all the steps in that process are right,</b>

103
00:06:20.875 --> 00:06:25.166
<b>we still end up with the wrong answer.</b>

104
00:06:25.166 --> 00:06:27.333
<b>This happens</b>

105
00:06:27.333 --> 00:06:28.375
<b>because</b>

106
00:06:28.375 --> 00:06:33.208
<b>we made a mistake in the initial step of</b>
<b>the process, took the wrong number</b>

107
00:06:33.208 --> 00:06:35.166
<b>or the wrong base,</b>

108
00:06:35.166 --> 00:06:40.416
<b>and this incorrect foundation,</b>
<b>despite following the right process,</b>

109
00:06:40.416 --> 00:06:43.708
<b>leads us in the wrong direction.</b>

110
00:06:43.708 --> 00:06:47.625
<b>Arjuna is making a similar mistake.</b>

111
00:06:47.625 --> 00:06:53.458
<b>He is failing to differentiate between</b>
<b>the physical body and the soul.</b>

112
00:06:53.458 --> 00:06:55.166
<b>And because of this, </b>

113
00:06:55.166 --> 00:06:57.416
<b>even though his arguments are sound,</b>

114
00:06:57.416 --> 00:07:02.333
<b>his overall situation is completely contradictory.</b>

115
00:07:02.333 --> 00:07:06.291
<b>The same paradox is prevalent in society today.</b>

116
00:07:06.291 --> 00:07:09.250
<b>We have all progressed in science,</b>

117
00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:15.291
<b>and new inventions are being made</b>
<b>to make human life easier.</b>

118
00:07:15.291 --> 00:07:16.208
<b>Then why</b>

119
00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:19.666
<b>is there so much emptiness in people's minds,</b>

120
00:07:19.666 --> 00:07:23.541
<b>why is there so much suffering?</b>

121
00:07:23.541 --> 00:07:26.666
<b>Because these inventions are material,</b>

122
00:07:26.666 --> 00:07:29.166
<b>our thinking is material,</b>

123
00:07:29.166 --> 00:07:36.250
<b>and the invisible, spiritual soul is</b>
<b>losing the attention of humans.</b>

124
00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:41.291
<b>The very existence of human beings is spiritual,</b>

125
00:07:41.291 --> 00:07:50.791
<b>and their thirst can only be quenched</b>
<b>by spirituality, not by material pleasures.</b>

126
00:07:50.791 --> 00:07:57.083
<b>If you lock a bird in a cage and provide it with</b>
<b>all the comforts and luxuries,</b>

127
00:07:57.083 --> 00:08:00.166
<b>give it delicious food,</b>

128
00:08:00.166 --> 00:08:01.416
<b>Yet,</b>

129
00:08:01.416 --> 00:08:10.125
<b>the day that cage opens, leaving behind</b>
<b>all these comforts,it will prefer to fly away.</b>

130
00:08:10.125 --> 00:08:11.375
<b>Similarly,</b>

131
00:08:11.375 --> 00:08:17.500
<b>human beings have confined themselves</b>
<b>within the cage of material life,</b>

132
00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:24.166
<b>while the key to that cage is already</b>
<b>with them, within them.</b>

133
00:08:24.166 --> 00:08:25.291
<b>It's their</b>

134
00:08:25.291 --> 00:08:27.208
<b>inner self.</b>

135
00:08:27.208 --> 00:08:30.458
<b>He is just unaware of this fact.</b>

136
00:08:30.458 --> 00:08:35.625
<b>These teachings of the Gita are</b>
<b>the path to reaching that key.</b>

137
00:08:36.166 --> 00:08:40.083


138
00:08:40.083 --> 00:08:41.958
<b>In professional life,</b>

139
00:08:41.958 --> 00:08:46.000
<b>we often encounter duplicity.</b>

140
00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.375
<b>Where someone's words may be very polite,</b>

141
00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:53.708
<b>and the goals shared in</b>
<b>those words may be excellent,</b>

142
00:08:53.708 --> 00:08:55.000
<b>but</b>

143
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.291
<b>when it comes to actions,</b>
<b>everything seems contrary.</b>

144
00:08:58.291 --> 00:08:59.958
<b>It is not necessarily true</b>

145
00:08:59.958 --> 00:09:05.666
<b>that those who are rich in words are</b>
<b>always rich in deeds as well.</b>

146
00:09:05.666 --> 00:09:08.958
<b>Here, two thoughts are worth keeping in mind.</b>

147
00:09:08.958 --> 00:09:10.458
<b>First thought</b>

148
00:09:10.458 --> 00:09:13.291
<b>Stay away from such hypocrisy,</b>

149
00:09:13.291 --> 00:09:15.541
<b>and if necessary,</b>

150
00:09:15.541 --> 00:09:20.041
<b>there is no harm in standing firm</b>
<b>against such behavior.</b>

151
00:09:20.041 --> 00:09:21.250
<b>But yes,</b>

152
00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:26.583
<b>just keep in mind that your conduct should be</b>
<b>within the bounds of decency.</b>

153
00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:29.166
<b>Second thought</b>

154
00:09:29.166 --> 00:09:31.833
<b>Give importance to those who are rich in deeds,</b>

155
00:09:31.833 --> 00:09:34.208
<b>not to those who are rich in words.</b>

156
00:09:34.208 --> 00:09:37.166
<b>Someone who excels in their work</b>

157
00:09:37.166 --> 00:09:37.750
<b>but</b>

158
00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.958
<b>cannot express it well</b>

159
00:09:40.958 --> 00:09:47.500
<b>is far superior to a hollow, eloquent colleague.</b>

160
00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:50.125
<b>Keep this in mind.</b>

